---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'Hair Length Calculator',
  applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any (Web)',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
---
<Layout
  title="Hair Length Calculator | How Long to Grow Your Hair"
  description="Estimate how many months it will take to grow your hair from its current length to your goal length."
  canonicalPath="/tools/hair-length-calculator/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14">
    <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mb-2"><a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a> / <a href="/tools/" class="hover:underline">Tools</a> / Hair Length Calculator</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Hair Length Calculator</h1>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      Enter your current and desired hair length to estimate how long it will take to
      grow it out, based on an adjustable average monthly growth rate.
    </p>

    <form id="length-form" class="border border-sand rounded-xl2 bg-white p-6 space-y-6">
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div>
          <label class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2" for="current-length">Current length (inches)</label>
          <input id="current-length" type="number" min="0" step="0.5" value="8" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-sand px-3 py-2 text-sm" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2" for="desired-length">Desired length (inches)</label>
          <input id="desired-length" type="number" min="0" step="0.5" value="14" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-sand px-3 py-2 text-sm" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <label class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2" for="growth-rate">Average monthly growth (inches)</label>
        <input id="growth-rate" type="number" min="0.1" step="0.05" value="0.5" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-sand px-3 py-2 text-sm" />
        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mt-1">Typical average is about 0.5 inch per month — adjust if you know your own rate.</p>
      </div>

      <button type="submit" class="w-full rounded-lg bg-rose-500 text-white font-medium py-3 hover:bg-rose-600 transition-colors">
        Calculate Growth Time
      </button>
    </form>

    <div id="length-result" class="hidden mt-6 border border-sand rounded-xl2 bg-rose-50 p-6 space-y-2">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold mb-1">Estimated Growth</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/70" id="length-diff"></p>
      <p class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-ink" id="length-months"></p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/70" id="length-weeks"></p>
      <p class="text-xs text-ink/60 mt-4">
        Hair growth varies between individuals based on genetics, health, hair care
        routine and other factors. This calculator provides a general estimate and
        should not be considered medical advice.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold mt-12 mb-3">How Hair Growth Actually Works</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-6">
      Hair grows from follicles in the scalp in a repeating cycle: an active
      growth phase that can last several years, followed by a brief transitional
      phase, and then a resting phase before the strand eventually sheds and a new
      one begins growing in its place. At any given time, the vast majority of
      your hair follicles are in the active growth phase, which is why hair
      generally grows at a fairly steady, predictable rate over the course of
      months — even though the exact rate varies from person to person.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Why the Default Rate Might Not Match You</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-6">
      Half an inch per month is a commonly cited average, but it's exactly that —
      an average, not a universal constant. Genetics play the largest role in your
      personal growth rate, but age, overall health, nutrition, and hormonal
      factors all contribute too. Hair growth also tends to slow slightly with
      age, and can be temporarily affected by significant stress, illness, or
      rapid changes in diet. If you've tracked your own hair growth over a few
      months with photos or measurements, use that number instead of the default —
      it will give you a far more accurate estimate than a generic average.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Why "Grown Length" Isn't Always What You See</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-6">
      One common source of frustration: hair can be growing at a completely normal
      rate while still not appearing to get any longer, because breakage at the
      ends is happening at roughly the same pace as new growth. If your hair
      doesn't seem to be gaining length despite months of growth, the more likely
      culprit is often breakage — from heat styling, chemical processing, or
      friction — rather than a slow growth rate. Addressing breakage (see our
      guide on <a href="/hair-care/dry-hair/" class="text-rose-600 underline">caring for dry hair</a>)
      often does more for visible length than trying to speed up growth itself,
      which is largely determined by genetics and not easily changed by products.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Planning Around a Growing-Out Period</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-6">
      This calculator is especially useful if you're growing out a shorter cut, an
      undercut, or bangs and want a realistic sense of when you'll hit a length
      you're happy with — and, just as importantly, when to schedule shaping trims
      along the way so the in-between stages look intentional rather than
      awkward. Bring your target timeline into your next salon visit and ask your
      stylist how they'd recommend trimming through the growing-out process.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">A Note on Supplements and "Growth" Products</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm">
      Plenty of products claim to speed up hair growth, but the underlying rate
      hair grows from the follicle is largely determined by genetics and overall
      health, not topical products. Some supplements may help if you have an
      actual nutritional deficiency contributing to slower growth or shedding,
      but that's a question for a doctor, not a marketing claim on a bottle. Use
      this calculator with your natural rate — adjusted honestly based on your
      own tracked history — rather than an optimistic number from a product
      label.
    </p>
  </section>

  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('length-form') as HTMLFormElement;
    const resultBox = document.getElementById('length-result');
    const diffEl = document.getElementById('length-diff');
    const monthsEl = document.getElementById('length-months');
    const weeksEl = document.getElementById('length-weeks');

    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const current = parseFloat((document.getElementById('current-length') as HTMLInputElement).value);
      const desired = parseFloat((document.getElementById('desired-length') as HTMLInputElement).value);
      const rate = parseFloat((document.getElementById('growth-rate') as HTMLInputElement).value);

      if (isNaN(current) || isNaN(desired) || isNaN(rate) || rate <= 0) {
        alert('Please enter valid numbers, with a growth rate greater than zero.');
        return;
      }

      const diff = desired - current;
      if (diffEl) {
        diffEl.textContent = diff <= 0
          ? `Your desired length (${desired}") is already at or shorter than your current length (${current}").`
          : `Difference: ${diff.toFixed(1)} inches`;
      }

      if (diff > 0) {
        const months = diff / rate;
        if (monthsEl) monthsEl.textContent = `≈ ${months.toFixed(1)} months`;
        if (weeksEl) weeksEl.textContent = `That's roughly ${(months * 4.345).toFixed(0)} weeks`;
      } else {
        if (monthsEl) monthsEl.textContent = '';
        if (weeksEl) weeksEl.textContent = '';
      }

      resultBox?.classList.remove('hidden');
      resultBox?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
